    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cf307f9d_7fcbeb20",
        "filename": "acme/acme.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 609,
      "author": {
        "id": 26521
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-06-07T15:12:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027d need to pull template from options (in case user provided one), or have the default in TLSxxxChallengeCert functions (in case not) instead of in tlsChallengeCert, and modify it and pass again. This is pretty cumbersome.",
      "parentUuid": "4c24b853_07b19372",
      "revId": "251eb89ed082142609e94393bbe87bc7af71f560",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ad27a4c1_25ea94aa",
        "filename": "acme/acme.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 609,
      "author": {
        "id": 6347
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-06-07T15:35:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, just append the acme extension to the user-specified template, or create a new one if none were specified. Not sure about \"have the default in TLSxxxChallengeCert functions\" - tlsChallengeCert already creates the default template.\n\nI don\u0027t see a problem here. What am I missing?",
      "parentUuid": "cf307f9d_7fcbeb20",
      "revId": "251eb89ed082142609e94393bbe87bc7af71f560",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f7023e8f_fb8bf7ad",
        "filename": "acme/acme.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 884,
      "author": {
        "id": 6347
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-06-07T14:43:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "if opt slice in tslChallengeCert args is empty, you\u0027re effectively zeroing ExtraExtensions. This was not the case before this change, where the value is \"... produced based on the other fields.\"\n\nSee the field docs in https://golang.org/pkg/crypto/x509/#Certificate.",
      "revId": "251eb89ed082142609e94393bbe87bc7af71f560",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c4ffa2e3_70246231",
        "filename": "acme/acme.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 884,
      "author": {
        "id": 26521
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-06-07T15:12:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You\u0027re right the semantic was strange. I\u0027ve modified it so that extensions from all WithExtensions options are added to the template instead.",
      "parentUuid": "f7023e8f_fb8bf7ad",
      "revId": "251eb89ed082142609e94393bbe87bc7af71f560",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "08cb6bcf_014772f1",
        "filename": "acme/acme.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 884,
      "author": {
        "id": 6347
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-06-07T15:35:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This seems to complicate things even more: if I specify a template the default semantics for ExtraExtensions hold. If I only specify the extra extensions, they override the default template\u0027s. If I specify both, my WithExtensions option gets appended to the other extra extensions I\u0027d specified in the template.\n\nI think it should be much simpler, and it feels like it can with using just the existing WithTemplate option.",
      "parentUuid": "c4ffa2e3_70246231",
      "revId": "251eb89ed082142609e94393bbe87bc7af71f560",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705",
      "unresolved": true
    },
